   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to written contracts for commercial applications",
    "basePrintNo": "S4363",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4363-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §33-1001, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4363\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to written\ncontracts for commercial applications\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo give certified lawn care professionals and the homeowners\nwith which they have contracted with the option of receiving their\ncontract in either paper or electronic format.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection one adds the option for property owners\nto receive an electronic copy of the required materials from\ncertified lawn care professionals with which they have contracted\nwith for pesticide application.\n\nSection two provides the enactment date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis law, first established in 1987, requires certified\npesticide applicators who enter into a contract with property owners\nto supply to the owners a written copy of the following: a list of\nsubstances to be applied including brand names and generic names of\nactive ingredients; any warnings that appear on the label of\npesticides to be applied that are pertinent to the protection of\nhumans, animals or the environment; and the company name, address,\ntelephone number, business registration number and applicator\ncertification identification card number. At the time, the only\nmeans by which this information could be presented to the property\nowner was in written format. This legislation would update this and\nallow for property owners to have the flexibility of receiving this\ninformation either in written format or electronically, such as on a\nCD or through email.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
